{"id":"mahabharata-3-176","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":176,"title":"षट्सप्तत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 176 · The python is Nahusha","summary":{"en":"The python reveals that he is King Nahusha, Bhima's ancestor, cast down from heaven by Agastya's curse for his pride, and that he will be freed only by one who can answer his questions. Meanwhile Yudhishthira, alarmed by omens, follows Bhima's trail and finds him in the snake's coils.","kn":"ಹೆಬ್ಬಾವು ತಾನು ಭೀಮನ ಪೂರ್ವಜ ನಹುಷರಾಜ, ಗರ್ವಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಅಗಸ್ತ್ಯಶಾಪದಿಂದ ಸ್ವರ್ಗದಿಂದ ಬಿದ್ದವನು, ತನ್ನ ಪ್ರಶ್ನೆಗಳಿಗೆ ಉತ್ತರಿಸುವವನಿಂದಲೇ ಮುಕ್ತಿ ಎಂದು ತಿಳಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಅಷ್ಟರಲ್ಲಿ ಅಪಶಕುನಗಳಿಂದ ಆತಂಕಗೊಂಡ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಭೀಮನ ಹೆಜ್ಜೆ ಹಿಡಿದು ಸರ್ಪದ ಸುರುಳಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಅವನನ್ನು ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अजगर बताता है कि वह भीम के पूर्वज राजा नहुष है, जो अहंकार के कारण अगस्त्य के शाप से स्वर्ग से गिरा, और केवल उसके प्रश्नों का उत्तर देने वाला ही उसे मुक्त करेगा। इस बीच अपशकुनों से चिन्तित युधिष्ठिर भीम के पदचिह्नों का पीछा कर उन्हें सर्प की कुण्डली में पाते हैं।","te":"కొండచిలువ తాను భీముని పూర్వీకుడు నహుషరాజునని, గర్వం వల్ల అగస్త్యుని శాపంతో స్వర్గం నుండి పడ్డానని, తన ప్రశ్నలకు బదులిచ్చేవాడే తనను విముక్తుని చేయగలడని చెబుతుంది. ఈలోగా అపశకునాలతో కలవరపడిన యుధిష్ఠిరుడు భీముని అడుగుజాడలు అనుసరించి సర్పపు చుట్టలలో అతనిని చూస్తాడు.","ta":"மலைப்பாம்பு தான் பீமனின் முன்னோர் நஹுஷ மன்னன், செருக்கால் அகஸ்த்யரின் சாபத்தால் ஸ்வர்க்கத்திலிருந்து வீழ்ந்தவன், தன் கேள்விகளுக்கு விடையளிப்பவனே விடுதலை தருவான் என்று வெளிப்படுத்துகிறது. இதற்கிடையில் அபசகுனங்களால் கலக்கமுற்ற யுதிஷ்டிரர் பீமனின் தடத்தைப் பின்தொடர்ந்து பாம்பின் சுருளில் அவனைக் காண்கிறார்.","ml":"ആ പെരുമ്പാമ്പ് താൻ ഭീമന്റെ പൂർവ്വികനായ നഹുഷരാജാവാണെന്ന് വെളിപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു; അഹങ്കാരത്താൽ അഗസ്ത്യശാപം ഏറ്റ് സ്വർഗ്ഗത്തിൽനിന്ന് വീണതാണെന്നും, തന്റെ ചോദ്യങ്ങൾക്ക് ഉത്തരം നൽകുന്നവന് മാത്രമേ മോചനം ലഭിക്കൂ എന്നും പറയുന്നു. അതിനിടെ അപശകുനങ്ങളിൽ ഭയന്ന യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ഭീമന്റെ പാത പിന്തുടർന്ന് അദ്ദേഹത്തെ പാമ്പിന്റെ ചുരുളിൽ കണ്ടെത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.176; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"आजगरपर्व","titleEn":"Ajagara Parva (The python)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स भीमसेनस्तेजस्वी तथा सर्पवशं गतः ।\nचिन्तयामास सर्पस्य वीर्यमत्यद्भुतं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus the mighty Bhimasena, fallen under the serpent's power, pondered the great and astonishing strength of the snake."}},{"n":2,"text":"उवाच च महासर्पं कामया ब्रूहि पन्नग ।\nकस्त्वं भो भुजगश्रेष्ठ किं मया च करिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said to the great serpent, \"Tell me willingly, serpent: who are you, best of snakes, and what will you do with me?"}},{"n":3,"text":"पाण्डवो भीमसेनोऽहं धर्मराजादनन्तरः ।\nनागायुतसमप्राणस्त्वया नीतः कथं वशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am Bhimasena the Pandava, next after the king of dharma, with the strength of ten thousand elephants. How have you brought me into your power?"}},{"n":4,"text":"सिंहाः केसरिणो व्याघ्रा महिषा वारणास्तथा ।\nसमागताश्च बहुशो निहताश्च मया मृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lions with manes, tigers, buffaloes and elephants have come against me many times and I have slain them in battle."}},{"n":5,"text":"दानवाश्च पिशाचाश्च राक्षसाश्च महाबलाः ।\nभुजवेगमशक्ता मे सोढुं पन्नगसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Danavas, pishachas and mighty rakshasas, best of serpents, could not bear the force of my arms."}},{"n":6,"text":"किं नु विद्याबलं किं वा वरदानमथो तव ।\nउद्योगमपि कुर्वाणो वशगोऽस्मि कृतस्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is it, some power of knowledge or some boon of yours, that though I strive I have been put in your power?"}},{"n":7,"text":"असत्यो विक्रमो नॄणामिति मे निश्चिता मतिः ।\nयथेदं मे त्वया नाग बलं प्रतिहतं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"My settled belief is that human valor is unreal, since you have blocked this great strength of mine, serpent.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"इत्येवंवादिनं वीरं भीममक्लिष्टकारिणम् ।\nभोगेन महता सर्पः समन्तात्पर्यवेष्टयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the hero Bhima, of untiring deeds, spoke so, the serpent wound its huge coils all around him."}},{"n":9,"text":"निगृह्य तं महाबाहुं ततः स भुजगस्तदा ।\nविमुच्यास्य भुजौ पीनाविदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having subdued the mighty-armed one, the serpent then released his thick arms and spoke these words."}},{"n":10,"text":"दिष्ट्या त्वं क्षुधितस्याद्य देवैर्भक्षो महाभुज ।\nदिष्ट्या कालस्य महतः प्रियाः प्राणा हि देहिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By good fortune, mighty-armed one, you have been given to me today by the gods as food when I am hungry. By good fortune, for the life of embodied beings is dear, in the great course of time."}},{"n":11,"text":"यथा त्विदं मया प्राप्तं भुजंगत्वमरिंदम ।\nतदवश्यं मया ख्याप्यं तवाद्य शृणु सत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"How I came to this serpent state, tamer of foes, I must tell you today. Listen, good man."}},{"n":12,"text":"इमामवस्थां संप्राप्तो ह्यहं कोपान्मनीषिणाम् ।\nशापस्यान्तं परिप्रेप्सुः सर्पस्य कथयामि तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have come to this condition through the anger of wise men, and, as a serpent seeking the end of the curse, I will tell it."}},{"n":13,"text":"नहुषो नाम राजर्षिर्व्यक्तं ते श्रोत्रमागतः ।\nतवैव पूर्वः पूर्वेषामायोर्वंशकरः सुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have surely heard of the royal sage Nahusha, the son of Ayu who founded his line, your own forefather among your ancestors."}},{"n":14,"text":"सोऽहं शापादगस्त्यस्य ब्राह्मणानवमन्य च ।\nइमामवस्थामापन्नः पश्य दैवमिदं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am he. Through Agastya's curse, for having disrespected brahmins, I have fallen into this state. See this working of fate in my case."}},{"n":15,"text":"त्वां चेदवध्यमायान्तमतीव प्रियदर्शनम् ।\nअहमद्योपयोक्ष्यामि विधानं पश्य यादृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you, whom I may not kill, come to me and are very dear to see, I will make use of you today. See what an arrangement this is."}},{"n":16,"text":"न हि मे मुच्यते कश्चित्कथंचिद्ग्रहणं गतः ।\nगजो वा महिषो वापि षष्ठे काले नरोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one once caught by me is ever freed, whether elephant or buffalo, at the sixth part of the day, best of men."}},{"n":17,"text":"नासि केवलसर्पेण तिर्यग्योनिषु वर्तता ।\nगृहीतः कौरवश्रेष्ठ वरदानमिदं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"But you have not been seized by a mere snake living among animal births, best of the Kauravas; this is a boon I have."}},{"n":18,"text":"पतता हि विमानाग्रान्मया शक्रासनाद्द्रुतम् ।\nकुरु शापान्तमित्युक्तो भगवान्मुनिसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I fell swiftly from the front of my celestial car, from Indra's seat, I begged the blessed best of sages, 'Put an end to the curse.'"}},{"n":19,"text":"स मामुवाच तेजस्वी कृपयाभिपरिप्लुतः ।\nमोक्षस्ते भविता राजन्कस्माच्चित्कालपर्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That radiant one, filled with compassion, said to me, 'You will be freed, O king, after some turning of time.'"}},{"n":20,"text":"ततोऽस्मि पतितो भूमौ न च मामजहात्स्मृतिः ।\nस्मार्तमस्ति पुराणं मे यथैवाधिगतं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I fell to earth, and my memory did not leave me; I remember the ancient events just as I learned them."}},{"n":21,"text":"यस्तु ते व्याहृतान्प्रश्नान्प्रतिब्रूयाद्विशेषवित् ।\nस त्वां मोक्षयिता शापादिति मामब्रवीदृषिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage told me, 'One who is discerning and answers the questions you put will free you from the curse.'"}},{"n":22,"text":"गृहीतस्य त्वया राजन्प्राणिनोऽपि बलीयसः ।\nसत्त्वभ्रंशोऽधिकस्यापि सर्वस्याशु भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When you have seized a creature, O king, even one stronger than you, the courage of everyone, even a greater one, will quickly fail."}},{"n":23,"text":"इति चाप्यहमश्रौषं वचस्तेषां दयावताम् ।\nमयि संजातहार्दानामथ तेऽन्तर्हिता द्विजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I also heard these words of those compassionate sages who had felt kindness for me, and then those brahmins vanished."}},{"n":24,"text":"सोऽहं परमदुष्कर्मा वसामि निरयेऽशुचौ ।\nसर्पयोनिमिमां प्राप्य कालाकाङ्क्षी महाद्युते ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I, who have done great wickedness, live in this foul hell, having taken on this serpent birth, O radiant one, awaiting the time.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"तमुवाच महाबाहुर्भीमसेनो भुजंगमम् ।\nन ते कुप्ये महासर्प न चात्मानं विगर्हये ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty-armed Bhimasena said to the serpent, \"Great serpent, I am not angry with you, nor do I blame myself."}},{"n":26,"text":"यस्मादभावी भावी वा मनुष्यः सुखदुःखयोः ।\nआगमे यदि वापाये न तत्र ग्लपयेन्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a man, whether he gains or not, in joy or sorrow, whether it comes or goes, the mind should not be dejected over it."}},{"n":27,"text":"दैवं पुरुषकारेण को निवर्तितुमर्हति ।\nदैवमेव परं मन्ये पुरुषार्थो निरर्थकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who can turn back fate by human effort? I think fate alone is supreme, and human exertion is futile."}},{"n":28,"text":"पश्य दैवोपघाताद्धि भुजवीर्यव्यपाश्रयम् ।\nइमामवस्थां संप्राप्तमनिमित्तमिहाद्य माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See how, through fate's blow, I who relied on the strength of my arms have come to this state today, for no reason."}},{"n":29,"text":"किं तु नाद्यानुशोचामि तथात्मानं विनाशितम् ।\nयथा तु विपिने न्यस्तान्भ्रातॄन्राज्यपरिच्युतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But I do not grieve for myself as destroyed so much as for my brothers, left in the wilderness, deprived of their kingdom."}},{"n":30,"text":"हिमवांश्च सुदुर्गोऽयं यक्षराक्षससंकुलः ।\nमां च ते समुदीक्षन्तः प्रपतिष्यन्ति विह्वलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This Himalaya is very hard to cross and full of yakshas and rakshasas. Looking for me, they will fall helpless."}},{"n":31,"text":"विनष्टमथ वा श्रुत्वा भविष्यन्ति निरुद्यमाः ।\nधर्मशीला मया ते हि बाध्यन्ते राज्यगृद्धिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or, hearing I am lost, they will lose all effort, for those lovers of dharma have been troubled by me, greedy for a kingdom."}},{"n":32,"text":"अथ वा नार्जुनो धीमान्विषादमुपयास्यति ।\nसर्वास्त्रविदनाधृष्यो देवगन्धर्वराक्षसैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or else wise Arjuna will not fall into despair: he knows all weapons and cannot be overcome by gods, gandharvas or rakshasas."}},{"n":33,"text":"समर्थः स महाबाहुरेकाह्ना सुमहाबलः ।\nदेवराजमपि स्थानात्प्रच्यावयितुमोजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"That mighty-armed, very strong one is able in a single day to dislodge even the king of the gods from his place by his power."}},{"n":34,"text":"किं पुनर्धृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्रं दुर्द्यूतदेविनम् ।\nविद्विष्टं सर्वलोकस्य दम्भलोभपरायणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How much more Dhritarashtra's son, who gambles badly, hated by the whole world and given to deceit and greed."}},{"n":35,"text":"मातरं चैव शोचामि कृपणां पुत्रगृद्धिनीम् ।\nयास्माकं नित्यमाशास्ते महत्त्वमधिकं परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I grieve for my mother, wretched and eager for her sons, who always hopes that we will rise above others."}},{"n":36,"text":"कथं नु तस्यानाथाया मद्विनाशाद्भुजंगम ।\nअफलास्ते भविष्यन्ति मयि सर्वे मनोरथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Serpent, with me destroyed, how will all those hopes of that helpless woman for me prove fruitless?"}},{"n":37,"text":"नकुलः सहदेवश्च यमजौ गुरुवर्तिनौ ।\nमद्बाहुबलसंस्तब्धौ नित्यं पुरुषमानिनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula and Sahadeva, the twins, who obey their elders, ever proud as men and sustained by the strength of my arms,"}},{"n":38,"text":"निरुत्साहौ भविष्येते भ्रष्टवीर्यपराक्रमौ ।\nमद्विनाशात्परिद्यूनाविति मे वर्तते मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"will lose heart and lose their vigor and valor, thoroughly stricken by my destruction. So I believe.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"एवंविधं बहु तदा विललाप वृकोदरः ।\nभुजंगभोगसंरुद्धो नाशकच्च विचेष्टितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this way and in many others Bhima lamented then, held in the serpent's coils and unable to move."}},{"n":40,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्तु कौन्तेय बभूवास्वस्थचेतनः ।\nअनिष्टदर्शनान्घोरानुत्पातान्परिचिन्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, became uneasy in mind, thinking of terrible portents with ill omens."}},{"n":41,"text":"दारुणं ह्यशिवं नादं शिवा दक्षिणतः स्थिता ।\nदीप्तायां दिशि वित्रस्ता रौति तस्याश्रमस्य ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"A she-jackal stood to the right and cried a dreadful, unlucky cry from the blazing quarter, frightened, at his hermitage."}},{"n":42,"text":"एकपक्षाक्षिचरणा वर्तिका घोरदर्शना ।\nरुधिरं वमन्ती ददृशे प्रत्यादित्यमपस्वरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A quail with one wing, one eye and one foot, of dreadful look, was seen vomiting blood, shrieking, facing the sun."}},{"n":43,"text":"प्रववावनिलो रूक्षश्चण्डः शर्करकर्षणः ।\nअपसव्यानि सर्वाणि मृगपक्षिरुतानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"A rough, fierce wind blew, dragging gravel, and the cries of all beasts and birds were on the wrong side."}},{"n":44,"text":"पृष्ठतो वायसः कृष्णो याहि याहीति वाशति ।\nमुहुर्मुहुः प्रस्फुरति दक्षिणोऽस्य भुजस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Behind him a black crow cried, \"Go, go,\" and his right arm kept throbbing again and again."}},{"n":45,"text":"हृदयं चरणश्चापि वामोऽस्य परिवर्तते ।\nसव्यस्याक्ष्णो विकारश्चाप्यनिष्टः समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"His heart and left foot also twitched, and an ominous disturbance arose in his left eye."}},{"n":46,"text":"स धर्मराजो मेधावी शङ्कमानो महद्भयम् ।\nद्रौपदीं परिपप्रच्छ क्व भीम इति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise king of dharma, suspecting a great danger, asked Draupadi, \"Where is Bhima?\" O Bharata."}},{"n":47,"text":"शशंस तस्मै पाञ्चाली चिरयातं वृकोदरम् ।\nस प्रतस्थे महाबाहुर्धौम्येन सहितो नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Panchali told him that Bhima had been gone a long time. The mighty-armed king set out with Dhaumya."}},{"n":48,"text":"द्रौपद्या रक्षणं कार्यमित्युवाच धनंजयम् ।\nनकुलं सहदेवं च व्यादिदेश द्विजान्प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He told Dhananjaya, \"Draupadi must be guarded,\" and he charged Nakula and Sahadeva to look after the brahmins."}},{"n":49,"text":"स तस्य पदमुन्नीय तस्मादेवाश्रमात्प्रभुः ।\nददर्श पृथिवीं चिह्नैर्भीमस्य परिचिह्निताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord traced Bhima's footprints from that same hermitage and saw the earth marked with his signs."}},{"n":50,"text":"धावतस्तस्य वीरस्य मृगार्थे वातरंहसः ।\nऊरुवातविनिर्भग्नान्द्रुमान्व्यावर्जितान्पथि ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw trees along the path broken and bent aside by the wind of the thighs of that hero, running swiftly as the wind after game."}},{"n":51,"text":"स गत्वा तैस्तदा चिह्नैर्ददर्श गिरिगह्वरे ।\nगृहीतं भुजगेन्द्रेण निश्चेष्टमनुजं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Following those signs he then saw, in a mountain cleft, his younger brother seized by the king of serpents and lying motionless."}}]}]}